//==
// # Discretized witnesses (complexity sweep, chunk L3)
//
// A model's edges discretized once per sweep, so a law over the table reads it instead of calling
// DiscretizeAll per case (testing strategy, part a; TKT-356). Layer 4's: every field is a layer 4
// type or lower, and no law over it needs a higher layer's model. The values are built in layer 8
// (08-pipeline/pipeline-discretized-witness.library.plato), whose witness criteria and layer 7
// models they use; the law runner builds every Witness_* of the type once, before any law runs,
// and exhausts the finite list for a law parameter of the type (it is not generatable: it holds a
// BrepModel).

// A model and the table DiscretizeAll makes for it under Criteria and Floors.
// Invariant: Discretizations is Model.DiscretizeAll(Criteria, Floors).
type DiscretizedWitness
{
    Name: String;
    Model: BrepModel;
    Criteria: DiscretizationCriteria;
    Floors: SegmentFloors;
    Discretizations: EdgeDiscretizations;
}
